From: Q8B SteamOS port <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: MGMT: fix backward compatibility with userspace

add_ext_adv_data() rejects the command unless the received length exactly
equals the length implied by the header (adv_data_len + scan_rsp_len).
That equality check was added by the CVE-2026-64126 fix to stop a
too-short payload from being read past its end.  The over-read only
happens when the payload is shorter than advertised, so the security
requirement is a lower bound, not an exact match.

Some bluetoothd releases (notably BlueZ 5.79 as shipped in the SteamOS
userspace) send the advertising data padded with trailing zero bytes and
set adv_data_len/scan_rsp_len to the meaningful length only.  The kernel
then computes expected_len < data_len and fails the command with
MGMT_STATUS_INVALID_PARAMS, which breaks BLE advertisement registration
and, with it, any client that depends on it.

Relax the check to a minimum-length check: still reject short payloads
(preserving the CVE-2026-64126 protection) but accept extra trailing
bytes, which are harmless to the advertising payload parser.

Signed-off-by: Q8B SteamOS port <noreply@localhost>
---
Backport of the upstream fix for BLE advertisement registration failing
with MGMT_STATUS_INVALID_PARAMS (0x0d) on radxa/linux-7.0.11.

Upstream fix: 149324fc762c2a7acef9c26790566f81f475e51f
  "Bluetooth: MGMT: Fix backward compatibility with userspace"
  Author: Luiz Augusto von Dentz <luiz.von.dentz@intel.com>
Regression:   d3f7d17960ed50df3a6709c5158caff989c8c905
  "Bluetooth: MGMT: validate Add Extended Advertising Data length"
Downstream:   58d810354de1b19d9af86a9829ad555d934a4866 (rpi-6.18.y, in 6.18.36)

On-board evidence and rationale:

Root cause (reproduced on-board 2026-10-09):
  - Steam Game Mode UI Bluetooth is unusable. steamui_system.txt repeats:
      YldStartAdvertising: failed:
      GDBus.Error:org.bluez.Error.Failed: Failed to register advertisement
  - bluetoothd src/advertising.c:add_client_complete():
      Failed to add advertisement: Invalid Parameters (0x0d)
  - btmon (root) shows the failing MGMT command is the data one:
      Add Extended Advertising Parameters (0x0054)  -> Success
      Add Extended Advertising Data       (0x0055)  -> Invalid Parameters (0x0d)
  - Raw 0x0055 payload captured via btsnoop is 18 bytes:
      instance=5, adv_data_len=0, scan_rsp_len=7, then 15 data bytes
      (the 7 meaningful bytes followed by 8 trailing zero bytes).
      Kernel computes struct_size = 3 + 0 + 7 = 10 != 18 -> reject.
  - Kernel side is otherwise healthy: btmgmt add-ext-adv-data with exact
    lengths succeeds; legacy btmgmt add-adv succeeds; hci0 is UP RUNNING.

This carries the upstream fix (149324fc762c) locally on
radxa/linux-7.0.11, which predates its merge, so the SteamOS 5.79
bluetoothd interoperates.  On-board verification (2026-10-09): after
deploying this patch (bluetooth.ko sha256 ad03e48f...), bluetoothd no
longer logs add_client_complete() Invalid Parameters and
YldStartAdvertising succeeds.
---
 net/bluetooth/mgmt.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/net/bluetooth/mgmt.c b/net/bluetooth/mgmt.c
index de5bd6b63..66fb5a187 100644
--- a/net/bluetooth/mgmt.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/mgmt.c
@@ -9115,7 +9115,7 @@ static int add_ext_adv_data(struct sock *sk, struct hci_dev *hdev, void *data,
 	BT_DBG("%s", hdev->name);
 
 	expected_len = struct_size(cp, data, cp->adv_data_len + cp->scan_rsp_len);
-	if (expected_len != data_len)
+	if (expected_len > data_len)
 		return mgmt_cmd_status(sk, hdev->id, MGMT_OP_ADD_EXT_ADV_DATA,
 				       MGMT_STATUS_INVALID_PARAMS);
 
